-- The Phase 5 BKM exhibit (DMN-EXPORT-PROGRAM-MODEL-SPEC.md §6.2): one module
-- holding, deliberately, one of each shape the emission must carry —
--
--   * a MULTI-PARAMETER tier-2 callee (`weighted sum`, arity 2), applied with
--     distinct argument shapes by a computed field and by another BKM;
--   * a BKM→BKM CHAIN (`boosted` calls `weighted sum`): the
--     knowledgeRequirement edge lives on the CALLING BKM (probe C1), never
--     hoisted to `case one`/`case two`;
--   * a BKM call INSIDE A HYDRATOR (§4.4 × §6.2, probes B1/B2): `Pay`'s
--     computed `total` becomes a boxed-context entry invoking the BKM with
--     earlier sibling entries as arguments;
--   * a λ-LIFTED CLOSURE (`adjusted` reads the module-level `baseline`):
--     measured 2026-08-01, a BKM body may read nothing beyond its parameters
--     (KIE refuses an unshadowed environment read at compile; Camunda answers
--     — the engines DISAGREE, so the lift is the only portable spelling), so
--     `baseline` becomes an extra formalParameter supplied at every call site
--     as `baseline: baseline`.
--
-- The two flavors emit byte-identical XML for this module (BKM emission is
-- ungated, §13.3; nothing here invokes a §), which the flavor-divergence test
-- in jl4/tests/DmnExport.hs asserts. The §-invocation half of the flavor
-- split lives in svc.l4, its own exhibit, precisely because an invocable §
-- makes the camunda flavor's golden unloadable on its own engine.
--
-- Engine cases: bkm.cases.json — run through BOTH engines by l4-cli-test
-- under L4_DMN_ENGINE_CHECK=1.

IMPORT prelude

§ `BKM exhibit`

DECLARE Pay HAS
    base  IS A NUMBER
    bonus IS A NUMBER
    total IS A NUMBER MEANS `weighted sum` base bonus

ASSUME pay IS A Pay

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`weighted sum` a b MEANS a TIMES 2 PLUS b

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`boosted` x MEANS `weighted sum` x 1 PLUS 1

GIVETH A NUMBER
`case one` MEANS `boosted` 10

GIVETH A NUMBER
`case two` MEANS `boosted` 20

GIVETH A NUMBER
`pay check` MEANS pay's total PLUS 3

GIVETH A NUMBER
`baseline` MEANS 7

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`adjusted` y MEANS y PLUS `baseline`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`adj one` MEANS `adjusted` 1

GIVETH A NUMBER
`adj two` MEANS `adjusted` 2
